<<<
+ origin, so that s. would mean a following, i.e. a company of followers; but the more generally known derivation is from Latin seco (cut).
===
+ origin, so that *s.* would mean a following, i.e. a company of followers; but the more generally known derivation is from Latin *seco* (cut).
